#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:5
#: 020c834026a94e5e893ce484fcf10d3e
msgid "Plane Architecture Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:7
#: d401185acd544b24a4856f81bac34eb1
msgid "This page attempts to roughly show the ArduPlane architecture.  Please note it was not written by Plane experts so there may be some inaccuraies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:12
#: 79928a3566b3433d893be1f54b5b0634
msgid "Above is a high level diagram of ArduPlane's architecture.  One large difference between Plane vs Copter and Rover is flight modes are not organised into a single file (:ref:`like they are in Copter <apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode>`) or class (:ref:`like they are in Rover <rover-adding-a-new-drive-mode>`).  Instead the code path goes through stages.  Each stage then decides what it should do based on the flight mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:14
#: 8db07a5697254839be45420392d3948a
msgid "These stages can be seen in the diagram above and include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:16
#: e0ae9cd2671e43be9e969436832c28b1
msgid "``ahrs_update`` calls the EKF to consume the latest sensor data and produce a attitude and position estimate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:17
#: 5d24d685004c4d2cb4a0f66b241c8f55
msgid "``read_radio`` reads in the pilot's input and calculates the appropriate attitude or position targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:18
#: 2dab7db741684cde8b13b15f9a6c67c1
msgid "``navigate`` calls the L1 and TECS controllers (see below) to convert position targets for the roll, pitch and throttle controllers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:19
#: 7e1681a261b44b7192c1aa9fcc7a85a3
msgid "``update_control_mode`` copies the L1 controller's roll and pitch targets to nav_roll_cd and nav_pitch_cd global variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:20
#: 0bc384edd9fa4ae09ad6ec0d198a44c8
msgid "``stabilize`` executes the lower level roll, pitch and throttle controllers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:21
#: bfb51b817bfb4f81899af7a6b6210958
msgid "``set_servos`` sends the output from the roll, pitch and throttle controllers to the appropriate servo outputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:24
#: 2d3c58ab7cc74fbaad80283ecbbb6f6f
msgid "Plane Controllers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:26
#: 957c7c1a6b4547eba88c10c98f8cb3ff
msgid "Plane has 2 high level controllers and at least 3 lower level controllers shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:31
#: 220dd4ea580c4865a26b294f9eda6061
msgid "the L1 controller converts a origin and destination (each expressed as a latitude, longitude) into a lateral acceleration to make the vehicle travel horizontally along the path from the origin to the destination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-architecture.rst:32
#: bbe98289eb7a4b479d64c33a2356f55d
msgid "the TECS (Total Energy Conservation System) controls the exchange between the vehicle's kinetic energy (i.e. speed) and its potential energy (i.e. altitude).  Its inputs are a target speed and height and it attempts to reach these targets by calculating target throttle and pitch values which are then passed to the lower level pitch and throttle controllers."
msgstr ""
